# Kamal secrets — resolved on the machine running `kamal deploy` (your laptop
# or the deploy CI runner), NOT on the VPS. This file holds NO secret values,
# only instructions for fetching them, so it is safe to commit.
#
# Secrets come from Bitwarden Secrets Manager via the `bws` CLI, authenticated
# with the BWS_ACCESS_TOKEN environment variable (a machine-account access
# token) — no interactive login. In CI it is provided as a GitHub Actions
# secret. This mirrors how the main Seurch app is deployed.
#
# The static docs site needs only one secret: the container-registry password.

# Fetch every secret the machine account can read, in a single call. To scope to
# one Secrets Manager project, replace "all" with "<project-id>/all".
SECRETS=$(kamal secrets fetch --adapter bitwarden-sm all)

# Container registry — a Scaleway API secret key with read/write access to the
# Container Registry (paired with the "nologin" username in config/deploy.yml).
KAMAL_REGISTRY_PASSWORD=$(kamal secrets extract KAMAL_REGISTRY_PASSWORD $SECRETS)
